<title>UK: Laura Ashley's Iverson calls in U.S. help - paper.</title>
<headline>Laura Ashley's Iverson calls in U.S. help - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ann Iverson, chief executive at ailing fashion and textiles group Laura Ashley Holdings Plc, has called in U.S. strategic consultants to restore the company's fortunes, a report in the Sunday Telegraph.</p>
<p>The U.S. Parthenon Group will focus on improving the group's supply chain, which have dogged Laura Ashley since Iverson's arrival in June 1995, the paper said.</p>
<p>The Sunday Times newspaper said Laura Ashley could face a bill of 100 million stg ($163.2 million) if it decides to abandon its foray into U.S. markets.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7717 ($ = 0.612 British Pounds)</p>
